Z||000000||speed racer||09-17-2001||10:34 PM||||What cars can I get the 3800 out of that will fit a fiero, dose it bolt strait up or do I have to make any mods. What are the specifications on it? How much would it cost for the motor and labor costs.<p>[This message has been edited by speed racer (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||AgaricX||09-18-2001||12:59 AM||||Well I got mine out of a '95 Camaro.  You'll have to fab the engine mounts.  You'll also have to use the Camaro ECU of course.  You can buy the mounts for 50ea or make them yourself.  I prefer the latter.  Labor anyone?  We did it ourselves, so I dont really know.  Its not horribly heard and is a great learning experience.<P>------------------<BR>85 SE 3800 Conversion (Currently 225HP)<BR>Body Work in Progress<BR>Pics to follow when it's not BUTT UGLY||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||09-18-2001||01:25 AM||||Speed,<P>If you are interested a friend of mine is selling a 5000 mile Supercharged 3800 from a GTP Grand Prix. You can e-mail Jeff at JLKHOTRODS@aol.com for all the info.<P>Rick 88||||reg||4
